PyQt-builder 1.16.4 works out the full Python library for --link-full-dll
(python312) but does not pass it to the linker, so Python.h links python3.dll,
which MO2 does not ship. mob patches builder.py for Mod Organizer 2.5.2 the
same way (patches/pyqt/builder.py.manual_patch); this is only its -l part.

--- builder.py
+++ builder.py
@@ -453,8 +453,9 @@ macx {
         # TODO: is this still necessary for Python v3.8?
         if not buildable.static:
             pro_lines.extend(['win32 {',
-                    '    LIBS += -L{}'.format(
-                            self.qmake_quote(project.py_pylib_dir)),
+                    '    LIBS += -L{}{}'.format(
+                            self.qmake_quote(project.py_pylib_dir),
+                            ' -l' + project.py_pylib_lib if project.py_pylib_lib else ''),
                     '}'])
 
         # Add any installables from the buildable.
